Description: elanmoc: set normal WBF mode (0x00) on 0c77 so user-space verify matches
 Windows leaves the ELAN:ARM-M4 0c77 in VBS WBF mode (set-mode 0x14
 value 1/protected), in which the on-chip matcher refuses every
 user-space verify with 0xfd "finger not enrolled" - even against a
 template Windows itself matches. The stock elanmoc driver sends
 set-mode value 0x03 at open and before identify, which keeps the
 chip in a protected mode on this FW. Sending value 0x00 (normal WBF
 mode) makes enroll and verify work; confirmed by hand via
 depau/elanpoc (set-mode 0x00 -> enroll -> "Recognized finger: 0").
 Only applied to ELANMOC_PROTO_V2 devices; other PIDs keep 0x03.
Author: local
Last-Update: 2026-06-12
--- a/libfprint/drivers/elanmoc/elanmoc.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elanmoc/elanmoc.c
@@ -815,7 +815,7 @@ elan_identify_run_state (FpiSsm *ssm, Fp
     case IDENTIFY_SET_MODE:
       fp_info ("elanmoc %s IDENTIFY_SET_MODE", __func__);
       cmd_buf = elanmoc_compose_cmd (&elanmoc_set_mod_cmd);
-      cmd_buf[3] = 0x03;
+      cmd_buf[3] = (fpi_device_get_driver_data (dev) == ELANMOC_PROTO_V2) ? 0x00 : 0x03;
       elanmoc_get_cmd (dev, cmd_buf, elanmoc_set_mod_cmd.cmd_len, elanmoc_set_mod_cmd.resp_len, 0, elanmoc_cmd_ack_cb);
       break;
 
@@ -1120,7 +1120,7 @@ dev_init_handler (FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice
 
     case DEV_SET_MODE:
       cmd_buf = elanmoc_compose_cmd (&elanmoc_set_mod_cmd);
-      cmd_buf[3] = 0x03;
+      cmd_buf[3] = (fpi_device_get_driver_data (dev) == ELANMOC_PROTO_V2) ? 0x00 : 0x03;
       elanmoc_get_cmd (dev, cmd_buf, elanmoc_set_mod_cmd.cmd_len, elanmoc_set_mod_cmd.resp_len, 0, elanmoc_cmd_ack_cb);
       break;
 
